+# AutoVideo 7.0.91: Flow reference identity by tile label, and a guarded shot resubmission
+
+## Why 7.0.90 did not fix shot_020
+
+Flow gave the two uploaded references (`location_master.jpg`, `character-aradhya-aaa37613-0`) new
+`/asb/` URLs on each project load. The 7.0.90 exclusion relied on the saved URL signature, so the
+references were not excluded. Each run downloaded them again, and the generation wait counted them as
+new output. Recovery then reported "No unique non-reference image yet" and stopped. The 7.0.90 early
+hand-off did not trigger, and the wait ran silently for the full 360 s.
+
+## What 7.0.91 changes
+
+1. **Stable reference identity.** Flow's tile label, `AV_<hash12>_<filename>`, is read from each probed
+   tile. When a probe is classified as an uploaded reference, its label is recorded in the journal.
+   Labels survive project reloads even when the URL changes.
+2. **Excluded from the wait.** Tiles with a recorded reference label are removed before the generation
+   wait counts candidates. Two real outputs are still blocked and reported.
+3. **No repeated downloads.** A reloaded reference that matches a recorded label reuses its saved bytes.
+   It is not downloaded again, and no duplicate probe files are created.
+4. **The wait says what it is doing.** A transactional wait prints its timeout and how many reference labels
+   it excluded at the start, so a long wait is no longer silent.
+5. **New tool: `tools/archive_uncertain_flow_image.py`.** It moves one unresolved shot journal aside so the
+   next Resume makes one new submission. It is never deleted, and it refuses when:
+   - the shot already has a downloaded image;
+   - the journal phase is not `submission_uncertain` or `submitted`;
+   - any saved probe is a valid image that is not a classified uploaded reference (recover it instead);
+   - the job is running (production lock held).
+   Without `--confirm-new-credit-spend` it only prints a dry run and changes nothing.
+
+## Steps for shot_020 (only after the user approves the credit spend)
+
+```
+python3 tools/archive_uncertain_flow_image.py outputs/20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729/storyboard/shot_020_open.jpg
+python3 tools/archive_uncertain_flow_image.py outputs/20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729/storyboard/shot_020_open.jpg --confirm-new-credit-spend
+```
+
+Then press Resume once. The old request is kept as `shot_020_open.jpg.flow-request.archived-<UTC>.json`
+beside the output. Do not press Resume again without a new approval.
+
+## Other notes
+
+- Default TTS split size remains 2400 characters.
+- `tools/update_v789_to_v790.py` is superseded and removed from `tools/`. The 7.0.90 zip still holds it.
+- Install with the updater from the 7.0.90 folder:
+  `python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.91/tools/update_v790_to_v791.py .` (dry run), then add `--apply`.
+
+## Verification status
+
+- Fixture tests only: `tests/test_v791_reference_labels.py` (13 tests) covers label parsing and exclusion,
+  reloaded references with new URLs (no re-download, no duplicate probes), labelled exclusion in the wait,
+  and the archive guards.
+- Full offline suite: 53 failed, 11 errors, 1397 passed, 44 skipped. The failures and errors are the same
+  environmental and pre-existing group as 7.0.90 (ffmpeg/ffprobe, typography, Streamlit). The suite is not green.
+- Updater round trip: 7.0.90 install to 7.0.91 with dry run, apply and an idempotent re-run; a 7.0.89 install is refused with the chain message.
+- Not verified against live Flow. The shot_020 outcome is unknown until the user runs the new submission.
